.TH smi-jenkins-controller "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Server Command"
.SH NAME
smi-jenkins-controller \- Start the Jenkins controller (WAR)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-jenkins-controller
.br
.B smi-jenkins-controller
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-home
.IR DIR ]
.RI [ JENKINS_ARGS\| .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-jenkins-controller
starts the Jenkins controller by running
.BR jenkins.war .
No options are required for normal use; sensible defaults are applied
automatically.
.PP
The wrapper translates
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOST
and
.SM SMI_JENKINS_PORT
into the native Jenkins WAR listener options
.RB ( \-\-httpListenAddress ,
.BR \-\-httpPort ).
The user does not need to know or supply those options.
.PP
Any Jenkins WAR arguments supplied after the wrapper options are passed
through unchanged, allowing full access to advanced Jenkins features.
.PP
JVM options may be supplied via the
.SM JAVA_OPTS
environment variable.
.SH MODES
.PP
The script selects its WAR, home directory and listen address automatically
from the effective user name, so the same command works on a developer
workstation and on a live installation.
.TP
.B jenkins
Live installation (rpm package, container image).
The WAR is
.BR /usr/share/java/jenkins.war ,
the home directory is
.SM JENKINS_HOME
or the jenkins user home directory when that variable is not set,
and the listen address is
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.B any other user
Development.
The WAR is located via
.BR smi-lib-location (1),
the home directory is
.BR ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins ,
and the listen address is
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.PP
The home directory is created when it does not exist, so the first start
needs no preparation.
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
In development mode the WAR is the one installed by the
.B jenkins
package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
smi-download-package jenkins
smi-install-package jenkins
.fi
.RE
.PP
.BR smi-install-package (1)
places
.BR jenkins.war ,
.B jenkins-cli.jar
and
.B jenkins-agent.jar
as root into the directory reported by
.BR smi-lib-location (1),
which is
.B /opt/setmy.info/lib
in a normal installation.
The developer never writes into that directory; all data is kept in the
home directory below the user own
.B ~/.setmy.info
directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Listen on
.IR HOST .
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOST
and the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Listen on
.IR PORT .
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_PORT
and the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
Jenkins home directory.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOME
and the built-in default.
Exported as
.SM JENKINS_HOME
before starting the WAR.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.PP
All other arguments are passed directly to
.BR jenkins.war .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOST
Listen address.
Default: mode dependent, see
.BR MODES .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_PORT
HTTP port.
Default:
.BR 7070 .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOME
Jenkins home directory, development mode only.
Default:
.BR ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins .
Translated to
.SM JENKINS_HOME
before the WAR starts.
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_WAR
WAR file.
Default: mode dependent, see
.BR MODES .
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Additional JVM options (e.g.\&
.BR "\-Xmx2g" ).
.SH PRECEDENCE
.PP
.B --host
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOST
> mode default
.PP
.B --port
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_PORT
> 7070
.PP
.B --home
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOME
> mode default
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start with all defaults:
.RS
.B smi-jenkins-controller
.RE
.PP
Listen on all interfaces, custom port:
.RS
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOST=0.0.0.0 SMI_JENKINS_PORT=8080 smi-jenkins-controller
.RE
.PP
Custom home directory:
.RS
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOME=/srv/jenkins smi-jenkins-controller
.RE
.PP
Pass a native Jenkins WAR option through:
.RS
.B smi-jenkins-controller --port 9090 --prefix=/jenkins
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins
Jenkins home directory in development mode.
Created when it does not exist.
.TP
.B ~/.setmy.info/.jenkins/nodes
Node directories, see
.BR smi-jenkins-node (1).
.TP
.B /opt/setmy.info/lib/jenkins.war
WAR used in development mode, installed by
.BR smi-install-package (1).
.TP
.B /usr/share/java/jenkins.war
WAR used in live mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-jenkins-node (1),
.BR jenkins-cli (1),
.BR smi-download-package (1),
.BR smi-install-package (1),
.BR smi-home-location (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
